    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0076" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.248/2–1645</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-16">February 16,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to invite reference to
                    Mr. Hull’s note of October 19, 1944,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d29-f1"/> concerning
                    the possible use by United States civil aircraft of airports constructed in the
                    Near and Middle East by the United States Government for military purposes.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The question of the use of the Anglo-Iranian Oil Company’s field at Abadan
                        has, of course, already been settled<anchor n="3" xml:id="d29-f2"/> but, in
                        general, I have the honour to state that His Majesty’s Government recognize
                        that questions relating to the use of the airfields are a matter for
                        discussion between the United States Government and the Near and Middle
                        Eastern Governments concerned.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I am further directed to explain that a reply to Mr. Hull’s note was
                        delayed pending the outcome of the Chicago Conference.</item>
                </list>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
